  "item": "R1",
  "scores": {"U": 2, "A": 2, "C": 3, "V": 1},
  "confidences": {"U": 0.9, "A": 0.95, "C": 0.8, "V": 0.98},
  "rationales": {"U":"'Registration Citizens can register their complaints with police' lacks subject clarity (who is 'Registration Citizens'?) and grammatical coherence; 'comp laint' contains a typographical error that impairs readability; the phrase 'take the comp laint forward' is vague and colloquial, not standard requirement language.", "A":"'based on the evidence, facts and following investigation' is ambiguous: 'evidence' and 'facts' are overlapping and undefined; 'following investigation' lacks temporal and procedural specificity (e.g., who investigates? within what timeframe? what constitutes completion?).", "C":"The requirement does not contradict known domain rules (e.g., citizens may file complaints with police), so correctness is moderately supported; however, 'shall take the complaint forward' is normatively weak and omits mandatory outcomes (e.g., acknowledgment, classification, referral), reducing fidelity to actual legal procedure.", "V":"No testable criterion is provided: no observable output (e.g., generated ticket ID, timestamped acknowledgment receipt), no measurable condition (e.g., within 24 hours), and no defined success state — 'take the complaint forward' cannot be objectively confirmed by testing or inspection."},
  "suggestions": {"U":"Citizens shall submit complaints to the police via the official web portal or designated counter; the system shall generate a unique complaint reference ID upon successful submission.", "A":"Upon receipt of a citizen-submitted complaint, the Police Complaint Intake Unit shall, within 1 business day, validate completeness, assign a priority level per Annex A, and either (a) initiate internal investigation if jurisdictional, or (b) forward to the appropriate authority with documented handover.", "C":"Keep as-is but augment with domain-accurate obligation: replace 'shall take the complaint forward' with 'shall either initiate investigation, refer to competent authority, or reject with written justification per Section 4.2 of the Police Complaint Handling Regulation 2023'.", "V":"The system shall record and return a human-readable complaint reference ID (format: CP-YYYY-NNNNN) and UTC timestamp within 5 seconds of submission; the police officer dashboard shall display the complaint status as 'Received' within 30 seconds of submission."},
  "issues": [
    {"type":"U","evidence":"Registration Citizens can register their complaints with police","rewrite":"Citizens shall submit complaints to the police via the official web portal or designated counter; the system shall generate a unique complaint reference ID upon successful submission."},
    {"type":"A","evidence":"based on the evidence, facts and following investigation, police shall take the comp laint forward","rewrite":"Upon receipt of a citizen-submitted complaint, the Police Complaint Intake Unit shall, within 1 business day, validate completeness, assign a priority level per Annex A, and either (a) initiate internal investigation if jurisdictional, or (b) forward to the appropriate authority with documented handover."},
    {"type":"V","evidence":"police shall take the comp laint forward","rewrite":"The system shall record and return a human-readable complaint reference ID (format: CP-YYYY-NNNNN) and UTC timestamp within 5 seconds of submission; the police officer dashboard shall display the complaint status as 'Received' within 30 seconds of submission."}
  ]
}
